Anthropic added <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/carplay/">CarPlay</a> integration to the Claude iOS app, which means Claude users can talk to Claude through their in-car infotainment systems.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1005142" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/06/CarPlay-Liquid-Glass-Light.jpg" alt="" width="1960" height="1102" /><br/>
Apple added support for third-party chatbots in &zwnj;CarPlay&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/18/ios-26-4-carplay-support/">in iOS 26.4</a>. Chatbot apps with &zwnj;CarPlay&zwnj; integration need to add support for a voice control screen, use Apple's designated &zwnj;CarPlay&zwnj; template, and get an entitlement from Apple. Claude can answer voice-based questions hands-free, but the chatbot won't be able to control vehicle or iPhone functions. Users also need to open the Claude app from the &zwnj;CarPlay&zwnj; interface because there is no support for third-party wake words.<br/>
<br/>
The Claude app on &zwnj;CarPlay&zwnj; opens with a "Start a hands-free conversation" screen, with options to start a new chat or access recent chats. There are in-app controls for muting and unmuting and ending and resuming conversations, plus visual cues for when Claude is listening or talking.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;CarPlay&zwnj; has long supported third-party apps, but Apple has limited the kinds of apps that are available to prevent driving distractions. OpenAI added &zwnj;CarPlay&zwnj; support to the ChatGPT app <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/31/openai-chatgpt-carplay/">earlier this year</a>.<br/>
